module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.coproduct_wire_contract_target_not_local_in_emitted_extdeps_github

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data coproduct_wire_contract_target_not_local_in_emitted_extdeps_github: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "coproduct_wire_contract_target_not_local_in_emitted_extdeps_github" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the emitter lowering a CoproductWireContract whose target coproduct is declared outside the emitting module, or the extdeps.github closure being emitted without that contract, so an emitted closure that reaches extdeps.github builds" } },

  receipts: [
    "**coproduct wire contract target not local in the emitted extdeps.github closure** (INVALID STATE: an emitted crate containing extdeps_github_github.rs whose CoproductWireContract names a coproduct, IssueState, that is not a local coproduct of the emitted module, so the target compiler refuses.",

    "HARM: any native claim program whose import closure reaches extdeps.github cannot be built, so its `gunbc test` label exits 2 with no observation; the wall that fires is cargo's, not the front end's (the .dag parsed and emitted 886 files).",

    "FILED FROM: `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:rfm-rung-census` at head 1bceac02818: V2-NATIVE REFUSAL cause=EmittedCompilerBuildFailed first_error=`CoproductWireContract target does not name a local coproduct: IssueState @ extdeps_github_github.rs:19:1`, 35 errors in v2-emitted-policy-unit-0. The reaching chain was gunbc.guarantee_stall -> gunbc.lifecycle_bounded_referent -> gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model -> gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_status -> extdeps.github.pulls -> extdeps.github.github.",

    "WORKED AROUND NOWHERE: the rung-ledger census avoided the closure by giving the trigger capability and blocker a referent-free home (gunbc.rung_climb), which is a modeling correction on its own merit and does not repair the emitter; the defect is unfixed and routed outside that change.",

    "MEASURED AGAIN, SAME INVALID STATE, DIFFERENT ROOT: `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli` on a tree carrying the new `plan-reference-migration` / `apply-reference-migration` CLI verbs (PR #16134, head 61fe111cae8): `V2-NATIVE REFUSAL cause=EmittedCompilerBuildFailed first_error=error: CoproductWireContract target does not name a local coproduct: IssueState @ .../extdeps_github_github.rs:19:1`, `error: could not compile `v2-emitted-policy-unit-1` (lib) due to 124 previous errors`, emission root src/v2/cli/compile_cli.dag, 612 files emitted, 18m59s wall. The reaching chain was the verb module's import of gunbc.generated_artifact_registry (for the generated-artifact ownership roster), which reaches gunbc.generated_artifact, gunbc.os_install and the fleet/deployment corpus: the closure of src/v2/cli/compile_cli.dag goes from 233 modules with none under extdeps.github to 582 with 11 under extdeps.github. The closure was only the exposure — the rows were already misfiled on main, and no emitted unit had yet been assembled that included them.",

    "CAUSE, AND IT IS NOT THE CLOSURE NOR THE FLOOR: the emitter composes a module M's contracts from the sidecar named M with the _contracts suffix (src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag contracts_items_for_module) and validates each composed contract against the coproducts LOCAL to M (emit_coproduct_wire_contract_target_validation, called with those composed items). Four rows sat in a sidecar that is not their coproduct's sibling, so they were composed into the wrong module and refused there. Moving a row into its coproduct's own module is NOT the repair: src/v2/workflow/floor_discovery_source_authority refuses a CoproductWireContract declared outside a `*_contracts.dag` file, and src/v2/workflow/floor_discovery_row.dag records the sidecar as a module-composition convention of the emitter. The repair is the placement the emitter already composes.",

    "AUDIT THAT FOUND THEM: every live `data <name>: CoproductWireContract = { ... }` read out of origin/main 8ca9a3a4419, comparing the row's module against its coproduct's `DeclarationRef { module_path }` with `_contracts` appended — 29 rows, 24 correctly homed, 5 misfiled: extdeps.github.github_contracts::issue_state_wire_contract (coproduct in extdeps.github.issues), extdeps.ebay.ebay_contracts::condition_wire_contract and ::format_type_wire_contract (coproducts in extdeps.ebay.inventory), extdeps.ebay.ebay_contracts::error_category_wire_contract (coproduct in extdeps.ebay.errors), and extdeps.systemd.systemd_contracts::systemd_unit_active_state_wire_contract, which is not a sibling of any module at all and is filed separately as gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.wire_contract_sidecar_that_is_no_modules_sibling_never_composed.",

    "CLIMB, AND THE RUNG IT REACHES: the four live rows moved to the sibling sidecar of the module that declares their coproduct (extdeps.github.issues_contracts, extdeps.ebay.inventory_contracts, extdeps.ebay.errors_contracts), with their comments and encodings unchanged and each coproduct's module importing its own sidecar as github.dag, checks.dag and pulls.dag already do. No emitter change, no floor change, no seed Rust: the defect was model placement, and the rung it reaches is the one where it was found — the emitted crate now builds, so the refusal no longer fires for this cause. The emitter's own lowering (the capability named in the standing above) stays unbuilt and this row stays open: an emitted closure may still reach a contract whose target is non-local, and nothing in the front end refuses it before cargo.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
